WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Question: how much does Manulife

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.890
Vitality save you? Answer:

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.080
welcome to Question an Actuary. I'm

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.750
Promod Sharma from Taxevity. If you want

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.490
to improve your health, you don't need

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.309
Manulife Vitality. Your smartphone likely

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:16.440
has a step counter. You'll find lots of

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.810
free apps like Google Fit. That's a good

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.240
start and may be enough. The heart of

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.060
Manulife Vitality is life insurance and

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.949
that comes at a price that's easy to

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:29.099
compare. Do you really save money? If so

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:32.279
how much? For this analysis, we'll look at

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:34.440
males and females; smokers and

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.120
non-smokers; ages 30, 40, 50 and 60. That's 16

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.370
combinations. We'll look at 1 million

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.070
dollars of Term 20. We'll compare prices

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.170
with Manulife Family Term and the

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.160
marketplace.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.469
There's more! We'll also look at the

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:51.210
effect of getting different coverage

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.360
amounts — 500,000, a million, five million

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.879
and 10 million — for a male nonsmoker age

00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:00.030
40. Caveat: term rates change and other

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.309
companies are creative too. What really

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:04.680
matters is the premium you pay at the

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.720
time you buy for the coverage that's

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.080
right for you. Notice all the green? That

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.939
shows that for 1 million dollars of

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:15.000
coverage, Family Term 20 with Vitality is

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.280
better than Family Term 20, as you would

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.979
expect. It's also the cheapest Term 20

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.049
product, except at age 30.

00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:24.570
Well done! What if you're looking for a

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.460
different amount of insurance?

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.950
This table is for a male nonsmoker age

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.770
40 and it shows the Family Term 20 with

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:34.200
Vitality is the cheapest choice for

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.750
coverage amounts of 500,000, a million

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:40.020
five million and 10 million. Buyer beware:

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.270
if you don't maintain your discount by

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.820
earning Gold status every year, you pay

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.369
the premium for Family Term 20 plus the

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:49.200
Vitality membership fee of two

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.170
dollars a month. Overall, Manulife

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.659
Vitality is worth considering: if you're

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:57.810
looking for Term 20 or Term 65; if you

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.270
like discounts; if you care about your

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.820
health; and if you get motivated by goals

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.219
and rewards. To explore your specific

00:02:05.219 --> 00:02:09.360
situation visit www.taxevity.com/vitality

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.030
and contact us. We can provide

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.470
official illustrations and

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.050
more details. Question: how much does

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:22.730
Manulife Vitality save you?

